I already know the answer to everything  it's just a question of getting to it  I'm Milton Glaser and I'm known as a  graphic designer  the issue about doing posters for urging  people to vote is that it's not enough  to say go vote you have to justify that  you have to tell people why they should  vote and that the why has to be a  powerful idea and I thought the idea  that voting is a manifestation of  existing and proving that you exist  because if you don't vote you're  essentially invisible and you don't  affect the structure of your own life or  anybody else's for that matter one of  the reasons that people don't vote is  they don't believe it will have an  effect and that is a great sadness  I have a hope that has in effect that  someone somewhere will be affected by it  and vote and if it's 10 people as better  if it's thousand people that's even  better  but the role of design is not to  persuade it's to inform if you try to  persuade people to do something that is  not in their own good you're committing  a dreadful act against the culture and  against civilization  you're doing something that is selfish  pigheaded stupid and ultimately  destructive the brain is a very valuable  instrument certain images certain icons  certain words have the power to  physically and spiritually change the  mind and it can be affected by colors  and shapes and sounds and images and  words in ways that we don't understand  art is essentially transformative a  single word or single gesture or a  single tool nor a single color can be  transformative
 

